# Monorepo Best Practices

This document outlines best practices for working with our monorepo structure, focusing on organization, dependency management, and development workflows.

## Repository Structure

- Organize code into logical groups:
  - `apps/`: Front-end applications
  - `packages/`: Shared libraries and utilities
  - `config/`: Shared configuration
  - `docs/`: Documentation
- Use consistent naming conventions across packages
- Maintain clear README files for each package
- Keep package.json files consistent and well-organized

## Dependency Management

- Use workspace protocols for internal dependencies (`workspace:*`)
- Hoist common dependencies to the root when possible
- Maintain a single version of each dependency across the repo
- Define clear peer dependencies to avoid version conflicts
- Use proper version ranges for external dependencies
- Document dependency decisions when necessary

## Development Workflow

- Set up consistent scripts across packages (build, test, lint, etc.)
- Configure proper task dependencies with Turborepo
- Use scoped commands for targeted development
- Implement efficient testing strategies for the monorepo
- Configure proper gitignore rules for generated files
- Use changesets or similar tools for versioning

## Shared Configuration

- Centralize common configuration (TypeScript, ESLint, etc.)
- Use composition for extending configurations
- Implement proper inheritance patterns for configs
- Maintain backward compatibility when changing shared configs
- Document configuration decisions

## CI/CD Integration

- Configure efficient CI workflows for the monorepo
- Use proper caching strategies for faster builds
- Implement incremental builds when possible
- Set up deployment pipelines for each application
- Use scoped testing to optimize CI runtime

## Code Sharing

- Extract reusable code into shared packages
- Implement clear interfaces for shared libraries
- Document API boundaries between packages
- Configure proper build order based on dependencies
- Use proper imports for shared code (absolute paths, etc.)
